      "head_commit": {
        "id": "5344e1b5924623ca2f13336a948d0ff13a7f6035",
        "tree_id": "3b7a6d426c2cb654352bb39e8d2978805605193f",
        "message": "Apply Grok quick-fixes: DSR bounded to [0,1], resolver hit-ts + per-pick price\n\nFour data-integrity fixes (GROK_20261022_1911_QUICKFIXES.MD) that were inflating\nP/L and confidence on /audit:\n\n1. Resolver intrabar hit path: bind pp_price up front (was NameError / stale\n   previous-pick price), stamp resolved_at with the actual hit-bar time instead\n   of the resolver run time (was the batch-close artifact), via new _hit_ts_iso.\n2. compute_deflated_sharpe: return the Bailey-Lopez de Prado DSR as a PROBABILITY\n   in [0,1], de-annualizing the Sharpe first. Old code returned a z-score on an\n   annualized Sharpe -> impossible values (DSR 7.69/14.71 in funnel data).\n3. _per_pick_price: price TIME_EXIT at the LATEST bar in [entry, as_of_ms] instead\n   of the first bar after entry (was stamping ~0.00% \"flat\" exits).\n4. strategy_verification_engine: pass n_trials=n_trials (strategy count), not\n   n (trade count), into the DSR call.\n\nTests: 3 new files (test_dsr_bounds, test_per_pick_price, test_resolver_hit_ts),\nall FAIL on main, PASS after. 43 resolver+new tests pass together.\n\nCo-Authored-By: Codebuff <noreply@codebuff.com>",
